    "title": "Fort Bragg opens new restaurant-style dining facility with healthier options for soldiers - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Justin Moore ,\n2 days ago FORT BRAGG, N.C. (WNCN) — Fort Bragg soldiers now have a new place to grab a meal, and it looks a lot less like a traditional Army chow hall. The Army officially opened the Rally Point Bistro Tuesday, Fort Bragg’s first campus-style dining venue. The new facility transforms a traditional military dining hall into a restaurant-style experience with multiple food stations, made-to-order meals, shakes, and a rotating menu featuring more than 3,000 recipes. Soldiers can also choose fresh fruits and vegetables grown locally each day. Read full article\n3",
